WEBVTT

00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:05.250
<i>In East Hand 2, Miyamori's 
Kosegawa had a haneman tsumo,</i>

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:07.480
<i>turning her score positive again in one go.</i>

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:09.360
Man.

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:12.740
If this keeps up, there'll be another penalty.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:16.450
You're pretty hard on Ueshige-san.

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:18.740
It's tough love.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:45.020
<b>The Nationals</b>

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:56.380
Fifteen months ago

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:59.340
Himematsu High School
 Osaka

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:04.070
<b>Hand 5: 
Gods and Demons</b>

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:04.770
Chi.

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:08.610
Suehara-chan!

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:11.840
Do you have a moment?

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:12.770
Sure.

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:16.250
What is it, substitute?

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:19.950
Oh, please don't call me that.

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:25.950
I'm trying my best to become 
an honest-to-goodness coach!

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:25.950
Himematsu High Mahjong Club 
Substitute Coach
 Akasaka Ikuno

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:31.750
Coach Zenno is still in the hospital.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:36.650
Don't you feel a little wrong about this?

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:41.880
I'm sorry.

00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:45.040
Anyway, what I wanted to talk about is...

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:49.520
I'm thinking of making you a 
regular for the team tournament.

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:51.020
I decline.

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:53.110
What?

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:55.910
Who else is on the team?

00:02:56.440 --> 00:03:00.970
For the third years, I have Nakagishi-san, 
Mino-san, and Umegaki-san.

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:02.040
For the second years,

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:07.090
I was thinking you and Atago-san's 
older sister could be good.

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:11.420
What about the first year 
Ueshige instead of me?

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:16.710
Is Ueshige that new girl 
who gets made fun of a lot?

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:19.270
She's so weak, though!

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:22.410
According to the standard 
rules we go by, she is.

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:27.540
But if you disregard the ranking bonuses 
and just go by the number of points won,

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.110
she's got a positive score.

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:31.730
And last month, she had the 
highest score in the club.

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:35.030
Even though she's usually last in the games?

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:36.950
That's bizarre.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:39.900
When she wins, it happens like an explosion.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:44.280
She scores higher, like 60,000 points, 
the stronger her opponent is.

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:46.850
Explosion, huh?

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:53.460
Then maybe I'll put her 
in the next A - B matches

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:55.610
and see how she does.

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:57.800
As long as she's not the fifth 
player, she should be fine.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:03.760
Please don't tell anyone 
I recommended her, though.

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:06.550
Why not?

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:13.690
Because it's embarassing.

00:04:13.910 --> 00:04:15.150
<i>The first players' match</i>

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:17.160
<i>is now in East Hand 3 of the first half.</i>

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:19.530
<i>Himematsu High School is the dealer.</i>

00:04:18.110 --> 00:04:19.530
Hey, hey.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:22.330
When's the exploding going to start?

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:24.530
She never did go off yesterday.

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:27.030
<i>Come on, Suzu-chan.</i>

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:30.560
<i>You'll show us, right?</i>

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:33.580
70 minutes later

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:36.100
First Players' Match
 Second Half 
South Hand 4

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:37.130
And we are in the last hand 
of the first players' match!

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:40.140
<i>Did you fail to go off again?</i>

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:43.990
Himematsu High School (South Osaka)
 2nd Year
 Ueshige Suzu

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:46.380
<i>Iwate and Nagano keep beating me down.</i>

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:02.480
<i>I've lost 24,300 points.</i>

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:02.590
Eisui Girls' (Kagoshima)
 2nd Year
 Jindai Komaki

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:04.530
<i>At this rate, we'll be in last place.</i>

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:12.470
Miyamori Girls' (Iwate)
 3rd Year
 Kosegawa Shiromi

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:15.990
<i>I managed to stay in the lead</i>

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:18.670
<i>throughout the second half.</i>

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:20.950
<i>This is all thanks to my training!</i>

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:21.150
Kiyosumi High School (Nagano)
 1st Year
 Kataoka Yuuki

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:24.860
<i>I got it!</i>

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:26.180
<i>This will seal the deal!</i>

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:31.510
<i>She's going to declare riichi.</i>

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:37.130
She fell asleep?

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:38.060
Oh...

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:40.310
Riichi!

00:05:58.360 --> 00:06:02.840
<i>In the first half, it was like 
something had vanished...</i>

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:04.870
<i>What is... this?</i>

00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:16.430
<i>The shrine priestess is back in scary mode.</i>

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:18.250
<i>This is kinda bad.</i>

00:06:23.350 --> 00:06:26.170
Kataoka does not get an ippatsu tsumo.

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:29.320
Pro player Kainou, Kataoka has declared riichi

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:31.080
even though she's in the lead.

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:32.480
Would you say this attack is...

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:34.830
Pro player Kainou?

00:06:35.890 --> 00:06:37.540
Something's taken over.

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:38.520
Excuse me?

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:49.630
Weird to say it now, but that's scary.

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:54.650
The shrine priestess has become a demon.

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:57.820
Deep in the mountains of Kagoshima,

00:06:57.820 --> 00:07:00.710
there is a magical realm 
where only female sages live.

00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:05.270
She might be someone who 
descended from there.

00:07:06.770 --> 00:07:09.690
Pushing through the many layers of clouds

00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:12.160
to make his way down from the heavens,

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:16.490
the god descended upon the Kushifuru 
peak of the mountain Takachiho

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:18.120
of Himuka in Tsukushi.

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:24.330
Ron.

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:27.550
24,000.

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:32.060
<i>The Princess who reigns over the</i>

00:07:32.060 --> 00:07:34.250
<i>six female sages of the Kirishima Shrine.</i>

00:07:36.170 --> 00:07:38.060
The first players' match is now over!

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:42.340
Eisui Girls' landed a direct 
sanbaiman hit on the leading

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:44.180
Kiyosumi High in the last hand.

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:46.210
Eisui Girls' (Kagoshima)
 1st Player - 2nd Year
 Jindai Komaki

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:47.190
With that, they leaped 
from last to second place.

00:07:47.850 --> 00:07:51.010
Currently in the lead is 
Iwate's Miyamori Girls'.

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:50.710
Miyamori Girls' (Iwate)
 1st Player - 3rd Year
 Kosegawa Shiromi

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:52.200
I'm tired.

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:54.440
The fight for the top eight spots now

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:56.700
moves into the second players' match.

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:03.990
Good job!

00:08:03.990 --> 00:08:04.960
Welcome back.

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:08.210
I'm back.

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:10.730
Kiyosumi High School (Nagano)
 1st Player - 1st Year
 Kataoka Yuuki

00:08:12.150 --> 00:08:15.280
It was a mistake to declare 
riichi when I was in the lead.

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:17.300
The riichi stick knocked me out of the lead.

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:18.570
What are you talking about?

00:08:18.570 --> 00:08:19.970
You did great!

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:23.090
A first year player went up against 
players from top schools,

00:08:23.090 --> 00:08:25.520
and came back with almost no points lost.

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:26.730
That is more than enough.

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:29.290
Leave the rest to us.

00:08:33.290 --> 00:08:36.820
The princess is still sleeping, right?

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:39.620
I didn't think she'd fall asleep again.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:41.080
It's rare.

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:44.920
Maybe Komaki-chan tried 
hard in her own way.

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:50.840
Do you mean she meant to fall asleep?

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:54.750
I don't think she's ever been 
able to do it on purpose.

00:08:56.390 --> 00:08:59.200
She's never played a public game where

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:02.270
a god didn't come down to possess her.

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:07.180
That's why she's never finished with a loss.

00:09:07.590 --> 00:09:12.280
Are you saying that maybe, this time, 
she was afraid that could happen

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:16.110
and something special got set in motion?

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:19.530
The princess always said 
that she started mahjong

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:21.760
so she could play with the six female sages

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:24.250
who are with her in the mansion of the shrine.

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:26.870
But now, her feelings are different.

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:28.220
She wants to win.

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:30.950
I suppose she wants to enjoy this

00:09:30.950 --> 00:09:34.460
tournament with us as long as she can.

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:43.190
In any case, if we win the tournament,

00:09:43.190 --> 00:09:45.260
it means we get to play with her the longest.

00:09:45.260 --> 00:09:47.930
That's right.

00:09:50.010 --> 00:09:52.730
Awai, it's your turn on camera.

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:54.610
Okay!

00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:57.590
Did something good happen to you?

00:09:57.590 --> 00:09:59.880
Did you feel it, Senpai?

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:00.980
Feel what?

00:10:00.980 --> 00:10:04.620
That there's some interesting 
people in this competition.

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:10.630
Interesting?

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:12.760
Doesn't that refer to you?

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:17.630
<i>It's nice to have a lot to look forward to.</i>

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:28.090
What are you sneaking around for?

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:34.250
I'm sorry!

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:35.480
Himematsu High School (South Osaka)
 1st Player - 2nd Year
 Ueshige Suzu

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:37.660
Oh, don't worry about it.

00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:39.070
That's how it goes.

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:40.860
Don't worry about it.

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:45.160
Oh, my! I forgot to bring the permanent marker.

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:45.780
Huh?

00:10:45.780 --> 00:10:47.410
Oh, well.

00:10:47.410 --> 00:10:49.000
I guess I'll use a normal marker.

00:10:50.050 --> 00:10:51.330
Seriously?!

00:10:51.330 --> 00:10:55.850
Suehara-chan, you prefer a permanent marker?

00:10:57.360 --> 00:11:00.840
I think I brought one!

00:11:01.610 --> 00:11:02.840
<i>You did?!</i>

00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:06.650
All right.

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:09.410
It's my turn.

00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:10.410
Yuuko.

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:13.810
It's okay!

00:11:14.830 --> 00:11:16.730
The exchange student from Iwate, right?

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:17.780
I know.

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:20.700
I've got the countermeasure

00:11:22.920 --> 00:11:25.030
for the Kiwi covered!

00:11:38.750 --> 00:11:40.850
Huh? Not going to talk to her?

00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:45.080
Well, I'm not really good 
with foreign languages...

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:48.690
But they speak English in New Zealand!

00:11:48.690 --> 00:11:50.880
Maybe my English isn't so good, either!

00:11:52.840 --> 00:11:53.650
Shiro!

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:56.410
Switch.

00:11:58.650 --> 00:12:00.650
Carry me.

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:08.430
Does that mean, "Get real"?

00:12:10.650 --> 00:12:11.950
I'm tired.

00:12:12.910 --> 00:12:14.330
All right.

00:12:14.970 --> 00:12:17.090
I'm heading off, then.

00:12:17.470 --> 00:12:18.800
Good luck!

00:12:19.170 --> 00:12:20.550
Do your best.

00:12:22.630 --> 00:12:24.320
I've got this.

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:38.060
This time, I'll really avenge you.

00:12:40.090 --> 00:12:41.070
Okay!

00:12:41.770 --> 00:12:43.420
Promise!

00:12:46.980 --> 00:12:48.660
The second players' match has started!

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:51.620
The starting dealer is first place Miyamori Girls'

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:53.370
Aislinn Wishart.

00:12:54.110 --> 00:12:57.680
The second player for the seeded 
school Eisui is Karijuku Tomoe.

00:12:57.680 --> 00:13:00.310
<i>Eisui Girls' is currently in second place.</i>

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:03.630
That Wishart-chan...

00:13:03.630 --> 00:13:05.980
She's kind of strange.

00:13:05.980 --> 00:13:09.140
Her play records didn't 
show anything strange.

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:12.180
Captain, are you blind?

00:13:12.480 --> 00:13:15.660
Her play records are pretty 
ordinary and her wins are, too,

00:13:15.660 --> 00:13:19.010
but she wins almost every hand.

00:13:19.010 --> 00:13:20.950
She had the highest win ratio in the nation

00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:22.250
in the regional tournament.

00:13:22.250 --> 00:13:23.780
That's pretty amazing.

00:13:24.190 --> 00:13:25.990
No matter how well you play,

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:29.280
hands that never get into tenpai 
are bound to happen.

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:32.940
But she has an abnormally high 
rate of being in a closed tenpai

00:13:32.940 --> 00:13:35.100
by the 13th turn.

00:13:35.890 --> 00:13:40.250
Her rate doesn't even compare 
to the normal average.

00:13:42.640 --> 00:13:45.080
Go A-chan!

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:47.240
Can I go home?

00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:48.930
Of course not.

00:13:49.960 --> 00:13:52.550
Aislinn's gonna win, anyway.

00:13:55.110 --> 00:14:00.310
<i>Aislinn materializes her own dreams, 
her ideal tiles, onto the table.</i>

00:14:39.200 --> 00:14:40.990
She looks like she's having fun!

00:14:40.990 --> 00:14:42.940
Looks like her regular pace.

00:14:43.930 --> 00:14:44.920
<i>Well...</i>

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:58.460
<i>When I passed them in the hall before,</i>

00:14:58.460 --> 00:15:01.480
<i>I didn't get that weird 
feeling that I got with Jindai.</i>

00:15:03.380 --> 00:15:05.220
<i>I don't think any</i>

00:15:06.980 --> 00:15:09.550
<i>of those three can beat Aislinn.</i>

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:21.060
Chi.

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:37.060
She threw away a tanpin iipeikou 
hand one tile from tenpai

00:15:37.060 --> 00:15:38.890
to go for a double-sided wait.

00:15:38.890 --> 00:15:40.870
Normally, it's unthinkable.

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:42.210
<i>Huh?</i>

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:43.380
Tsumo!

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:46.460
300, 500.

00:15:47.330 --> 00:15:49.090
<i>She called for </i>that<i> hand?</i>

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:52.970
<i>This is weird!</i>

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:54.420
<i>I had to do it.</i>

00:15:54.420 --> 00:15:57.100
<i>I had this feeling like 
the dealer might win.</i>

00:15:58.040 --> 00:15:59.380
<i>I've rarely ever been wrong</i>

00:15:59.380 --> 00:16:02.350
<i>when I've had this kind of feeling.</i>

00:16:02.390 --> 00:16:04.870
East Hand 2

00:16:02.390 --> 00:16:04.870
Dealer: Mase Yuuko

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:24.900
<i>I got this!</i>

00:16:28.730 --> 00:16:29.510
<i>Yup!</i>

00:16:57.460 --> 00:17:00.990
<i>Again it seems like the exchange 
student is about to win.</i>

00:17:04.590 --> 00:17:07.920
Huh? And why the red one?

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:08.790
Pon!

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:13.840
That's a lot of dora!

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:24.220
What was the name of the school 
with the sailor outfit again?

00:17:24.220 --> 00:17:25.530
Kiyosumi!

00:17:25.530 --> 00:17:27.850
It's the same school as Haramura-san.

00:17:29.780 --> 00:17:31.440
Kiyosumi, huh?

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:35.900
Turn 10

00:17:40.490 --> 00:17:42.460
<i>I don't want to pay 18,000,</i>

00:17:42.460 --> 00:17:44.570
<i>and the hand's almost over.</i>

00:17:44.570 --> 00:17:46.500
<i>All the 2 of circles are visible anyway...</i>

00:17:46.810 --> 00:17:50.300
<i>I guess I can get away with the 
dealer's safe tile, the 3 of circles.</i>

00:17:52.440 --> 00:17:53.170
Ron.

00:17:55.020 --> 00:17:57.630
<i>But she discarded a red 5 earlier!</i>

00:17:57.630 --> 00:17:59.140
2,000.

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:01.220
<i>Why is she winning with a hand like that?</i>

00:18:01.220 --> 00:18:03.350
<i>I don't get this at all!</i>

00:18:05.790 --> 00:18:07.630
<i>I probably would've been beaten</i>

00:18:07.630 --> 00:18:09.730
<i>if I'd played my regular game just now.</i>

00:18:09.730 --> 00:18:12.860
<i>Yup, I could already tell.</i>

00:18:13.290 --> 00:18:16.610
<i>It's not that Mako remembers 
all of the outcomes.</i>

00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:18.540
<i>It's more that she can remember</i>

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:22.190
<i>the overall layout of the table in the 
same way you'd remember someone's face.</i>

00:18:24.520 --> 00:18:25.500
A face?

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:26.820
Yeah.

00:18:26.820 --> 00:18:31.210
I think of the discards, or more like 
the entire table, as a person's face.

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:35.220
If it's a face I don't like,

00:18:35.220 --> 00:18:37.230
that is to say, if it's disadvantageous to me,

00:18:37.230 --> 00:18:39.600
I just have to make it into a face I like.

00:18:40.370 --> 00:18:43.010
It's just a matter of 
changing the table's layout.

00:18:44.690 --> 00:18:46.940
<i>Whether it's superstition or something else...</i>

00:18:46.940 --> 00:18:50.550
<i>If they can only make faces 
that Mako knows all too well...</i>

00:18:51.600 --> 00:18:52.910
<i>Why?</i>

00:18:54.840 --> 00:18:57.110
I forgot to take off my glasses.

00:18:59.830 --> 00:19:02.830
<i>Mako won't lose that easily.</i>

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:06.000
The second players' match has now moved

00:19:06.000 --> 00:19:07.410
into the last hand of the second half.

00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:13.170
Kiyosumi started the match in third 
place, but is now in the lead.

00:19:30.370 --> 00:19:31.510
<i>Wait!</i>

00:19:44.400 --> 00:19:45.230
Chi.

00:19:51.190 --> 00:19:52.330
<i>Why?</i>

00:19:58.020 --> 00:19:59.310
<i>One more time!</i>

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:07.270
<i>I can still do this.</i>

00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:13.770
Pon.

00:20:26.310 --> 00:20:27.070
Ron.

00:20:28.470 --> 00:20:29.790
3,900.

00:20:30.420 --> 00:20:32.460
And that's it.

00:20:33.510 --> 00:20:35.220
The second players' match is over!

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:40.570
Kiyosumi High School's Somiya ends 
the last hand with a 3,900 win.

00:20:40.570 --> 00:20:43.150
Her team will start the third 
players' match in first place.

00:20:41.880 --> 00:20:45.220
Kiyosumi High School
 2nd Player - 2nd Year
 Somiya Mako

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:45.220
Good game.

00:20:45.490 --> 00:20:46.890
She did it!

00:20:47.250 --> 00:20:49.270
Somiya-senpai!

00:20:52.570 --> 00:20:56.480
Though Miyamori Girls' Aislinn 
was overtaken by Kiyosumi,

00:20:55.290 --> 00:20:56.480
A-chan...

00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:59.290
they are now in second 
place with 103,500 points.

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:01.990
Miyamori Girls'
 2nd Player - 3rd Year
 Aislinn Wishart

00:21:02.590 --> 00:21:06.480
Eisui Girls' Karijuku falls one place to third.

00:21:06.480 --> 00:21:08.110
Good game, everybody.

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:08.990
Eisui Girls'
 2nd Player - 3rd Year
 Karijuku Tomoe

00:21:09.620 --> 00:21:13.290
It looks like we mustn't 
underestimate Kiyosumi High School.

00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:15.970
We're counting on you, Haru-chan.

00:21:18.410 --> 00:21:20.040
I got it.

00:21:20.040 --> 00:21:22.250
Good job, everyone!

00:21:21.550 --> 00:21:26.550
Himematsu High School
 2nd Player - 3rd Year
 Mase Yuuko

00:21:22.250 --> 00:21:24.090
Himematsu High School's Mase

00:21:24.090 --> 00:21:26.550
has played consistently 
well throughout the match.

00:21:26.880 --> 00:21:28.770
While they are still in last place,

00:21:28.770 --> 00:21:30.800
the distance between them 
and third place has shrunk.

00:21:30.800 --> 00:21:32.730
Good ol' Mase-senpai.

00:21:32.730 --> 00:21:34.270
You can count on her.

00:21:35.130 --> 00:21:36.520
All right!

00:21:36.690 --> 00:21:40.940
<b>Unripe</b>

00:21:36.800 --> 00:21:40.120
Looks like they've warmed things up well for me.

00:21:41.460 --> 00:21:47.260
Now I'm going to show them 
something from another league!
